path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Installation of six solar panel roofs across 6 Council’s buildings: Building 150 (Greenham Common) 18.70kWp, The Poenix Centre 43.52kWp, Markt Street Council Offices 99.29kWp, Aldermaston Primary School 45.56kWp, Willink School 191.08kWp, Willink Leisure Centre 48.96kWp.</p></div></details><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#fabe80;color:#111827;border:1px solid rgba(17,24,39,.10);">Pollution Prevention and Control</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Lighting upgrades</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£100,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Replacing 217 steel lighting columns with fully recyclable aluminium columns which have twice the life span of steel columns.</p></div></details><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#b191cb;color:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25);">Climate Change Adaptation</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Natural flood defences</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£100,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Tree and hedge row planting as part of the Dunstan Green, Siege Cross Park, Floral Way Reservoir to protect over 570 properties whilst creating habitats for local wildlife.</p></div></details></div></section></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-scope"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs bg-colour--primary-surface ai-past-wrap ai-scope"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div id="ai-past-investments"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm">Investment history</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><div class="ai-past-table-choke"><table class="brand-table"><caption>Investment history</caption><thead><tr><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Investment</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Interest</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Term</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Amount raised</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Close date</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td headers="investment" data-title="Investment"><a href="https://www.abundanceinvestment.com/invest/west-berkshire-2025" target="_blank" rel="noopener">West Berkshire 2025</a></td><td headers="interest" data-title="Interest">1.2% p.a.</td><td headers="term" data-title="Term">5 years</td><td headers="amount" data-title="Amount raised">£1,000,000</td><td headers="close date" data-title="Close date">10 October 2020</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex ai-scope"></div><section class="home-financial m-y-spacer-md p-y-spacer-xl mx-auto choke-800 ai-scope"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center" data-content="1-143095">Delivering net zero carbon across the community</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-lg"><span data-content="2-143105"><span>West Berkshire Council's refreshed&nbsp;<span><a href="https://www.westberks.gov.uk/media/64372/Environment-Strategy-Refresh-2025-2030/pdf/Environment_Strategy_Refresh_2025_FINAL_for_website_1uu4kxsr1adid.pdf?m=1755521813210" target="_blank" rel="" title="Link: https://www.westberks.gov.uk/media/64372/Environment-Strategy-Refresh-2025-2030/pdf/Environment_Strategy_Refresh_2025_FINAL_for_website_1uu4kxsr1adid.pdf?m=1755521813210">Environment Strategy [2MB]</a>&nbsp;</span>outlines the steps it intends to take with its partners to reach its target of net zero carbon for the council, and to play its part in working towards net zero for the district as soon as practicable.<br></span><span><br>The council believes that climate change is a serious threat, and it must act now if it is to respond to the danger this poses to our people, our wildlife and our environment. Its ambitious Environment Strategy&nbsp;highlights the fact that everyone in the community has a part to play in responding to this challenge.</span></span></p></div><div class="flex flex-center"><figure class="brand-figure w-100"><img src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/30907f04-5b47-47bf-9082-662770a3fbde.jpg" width="800" height="450" alt="Title placeholder text" loading="lazy"> <figcaption data-content="2-143108">Investors money has helped fund green energy projects like this one.</figcaption></figure></div></div></div></div></section></div>
